<!--Post: 10763--><!--Time: 1110219291-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10763"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 10:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let&#39;s throw THIS open to discussion. It&#39;s reported in Time Magazine his family has failed to even initiate contact with Dennis since he went to the pokey &#40;aptly named&#41;. <BR> <BR>Why would this be? Did SOMEONE in the household have an inkling and they are SO VERY GLAD to be ridst of his domineering evil? <BR> <BR>Are they just throwing in the towel and going on the premise he is BTK and they are ashamed to have ANY contact with him? <BR> <BR>Are they SO SHOCKED and DUMBFOUNDED they don&#39;t know what to do? <BR> <BR>Nary a phone call from wife or kids----this IS interesting as to why. Two weeks and NOTHING... <BR> <BR>Discuss----<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10763-->
<!--Post: 10765--><!--Time: 1110221384-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10765"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Miss<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Miss<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 10:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am so curious about this too.  We&#39;ve heard such conflicting reports about his personality, I&#39;m very curious as to what side of him his family saw.   <BR> <BR>I&#39;m kind of surprised that he doesn&#39;t have a criminal record for domestic violence.  It seems like control and domination are so important to him that it&#39;s hard to imagine his faimly avoided his wrath.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10765-->
<!--Post: 10769--><!--Time: 1110223478-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10769"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 11:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe the family must be in a state of shock, P. and the children are most likely hiding from the press at this point, I don&#39;t think  I would go see him at this time myself if he was my husband, I would be asking the same question as everyone else. Why? But I am not so sure I would want to know that answer or the other side of the man I thought I knew all these years. Once she gets gets thru the seven stages of grief, she may then go ask him why he did it. She may also be blaming herself at this point for not knowing<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10769-->
<!--Post: 10779--><!--Time: 1110226375-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10779"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I still believe that he was abused as a child sprinkled with bipolar disease.  My experience with bipolar family members has shown them to be very manipulative and sadistic &#40;either physicially or mentally or both&#41;. <BR> <BR>That being said, I fully believe that he was abusive to his family.  I also agree with the profile in that his wife was probably submissive.  She probably was terrified most of the time as were her children.  I don&#39;t think that she thought he was capable of being BTK, but very fearful of him nonetheless. <BR> <BR>Given that underlying scenario, add in his &#34;official&#34; duties and the church community.  She was probably afraid of embarrassment either for herself or her children.  Also, she didn&#39;t make a whole bunch of money as a cashier &#40;I imagine&#41; and was unable to support herself and her children.   <BR> <BR>That&#39;s why no one was ever alerted to the &#34;secret in the house,&#34; so to speak.   <BR> <BR>Also, I used to have a friend whose step father was a security guard.  He was very buddy, buddy with the police dept.  Well, I spent the night one night when he beat the crap out of my friend&#39;s mom.  I ran out of the house and he yelled at me, &#34;go ahead, call the cops...they won&#39;t do anything to me.&#34;  And he was right..they didn&#39;t. <BR> <BR>Even though BTK taunted and hated the WPD, I bet he was buddy, buddy with a few officers &#40;part of the manipulative characteristic of bipolarism&#41;.  Either that, or he had cop friends from church or boy scouts.  I&#39;d be willing to bet money on it. <BR> <BR>So, what I am trying to say is, I think his family is relieved in a way, but also devastated and thus, no contact.  I seriously doubt they will ever &#34;come out&#34; and talk with the media or anyone.  That&#39;ll take years and years of therapy and/or personal forgiveness.   <BR> <BR>I totally forgive them.  Abusers are monsters..they can make you think the sky is yellow when you KNOW it is blue.  I really, really feel sorry for them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10779-->
<!--Post: 10800--><!--Time: 1110231599-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10800"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 1:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Surf, I agree, I also believe if we can see Police Records we will find they were called to his house a few times for DV, But nothing happened and I have two children in my care both with Bi Polar and and eight year old son with ADD so I see everyday how quickly a person can change from one min. to the next, If they were not in Therapy and on medication, they would be a lot to handle, I also remember in the 70&#39;s when police didn&#39;t take DV the way they do now, It was known In my family at least, that your wife and children were your property so to speak and Rape and abuse was a hidden family matter. I hope no matter what else the family does, that they at least get some kind of help<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10800-->
<!--Post: 10812--><!--Time: 1110237422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10812"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 3:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found this article that offers a little insight into the Raders childhood. <BR> <BR>BTK&#39;s brother interview by FBI <BR> <BR>&#34;The first questions were, who&#39;s your mother, your brothers, your grandparents and so on,&#34; Jeff Rader said. &#34;Then they asked: Does your brother have a fascination with trains? <BR> <BR>&#34;Not that I know of,&#34; Jeff Rader told them. &#34;But I do. I used to play on trains at the train yard when I was a kid. I love trains.&#34; <BR>The four brothers &#40;Dennis is the eldest&#41; grew up with a loving mother and a tough but decent father, he said. <BR> <BR>Their father, William Rader, was a former Marine, a God-fearing man, strict but not unreasonable. He died in 1996. <BR> <BR>&#34;All four boys became Boy Scouts,&#34; Jeff Rader said. &#34;We were a normal family. The boys all liked to be outdoors, go for hikes. We loved to hunt and fish.&#34; <BR> <BR>There was no trouble in the family, no abuse, he said. <BR> <BR>He said his brother was a good kid. <BR> <BR>&#34;I wasn&#39;t,&#34; Jeff said. <BR> <BR>&#34;I was a hell-raiser. But Dennis wasn&#39;t. Dennis and his wife, Paula, came to this house often to look after his mother, Jeff said. His brother often took the lead on that, driving their mother to the doctor when needed. <BR> <BR>When the January ice storm knocked out power to tens of thousands of people, Jeff said, Dennis and his wife came over and stayed with his mother for a week, until power was restored to their house <BR> <BR>They grew up having fun, he said. &#34;We had a loving mother, and a loving father.&#34; <BR> <BR>He said both those parents tried to teach them to be religious. <BR> <BR>And to know the difference between right and wrong.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10812-->
