</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 10:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have tried to imagine being in this situation, me I probably would smack him, but B you are right, what is there to say, Which brings up a good point, when the police ask the daughter for her DNA, do you think she called her brother or her mom? How could you keep that to yourself<!--/Text--></td></tr>
