<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10882"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 11:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E: I believe they obtained her DNA from a doctor in Wichita that she had seen. They don&#39;t have to get a signed HIPPA form for medical records if it involves a criminal investigation. &#40;Subpoena&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
